P31-N is now proved with the explicit bound
\[
\rho_L\le \frac{4}{3\sqrt3}\left(1+\frac{2}{\sqrt{L+1}}\right)^3.
\]
I also proved the elementary uniform bound \(\rho_L\le0.95\) for every \(L\ge1\); \(L=0\) remains the exact exception.

The VM tests found no violation across intervals, random and tapered sets, lacunary sets, dense cores with sparse tails, Singer/Bu examples, and the two dense records. I also found a directly relevant 1996 paper on dense cosine sums and am checking how much of P29/P31 it covers.
